#LESSON 4 on Exceptions

#Exceptions are a way to report that something went wrong while code was running and instead of letting the error end the execution define responses
#try: contains the code that may fail 
#except: handles particular type of failure
#else: runs only if the try block succeeds
#finally: runs regardless of success or failure (for cleanup

#Exception handling is not about preventing every possible error. It is about distinguishing:
#Expected operational failures that your program should handle (e.g. as invalid input)
#Programming bugs that should remain visible so you can fix them
#Exceptions refer to problems in the code 


